# Ollama: pinned build inputs (read by apps/ollama/build.sh).
#
# Plain KEY=VALUE lines only (no shell expansion, no command substitution): build.sh parses this file strictly.
#
# The app ships Ollama's own release binary for linux-arm64; nothing is compiled. build.sh downloads the release asset, checks its
# SHA-256 against BOTH the sha256sum.txt that the release publishes AND the value pinned here (so a swapped asset, or a swapped
# checksum file, is caught), and only then unpacks it.
#
# Why 0.35.0: the newest release that was published and tagged at least 14 days before 2026-10-15 by every date GitHub shows
# (v0.35.0: published and committed 2026-09-28). v0.35.1 (commit 2026-10-02) and v0.40.0 (commit 2026-10-06, although published
# 2026-09-25) are younger by their commit date, v0.40.1 and later by every date. To move the pin: change the three values below
# (OLLAMA_ASSET_SHA256 comes from the release's sha256sum.txt), then run build.sh and tests/apps/ollama.mjs.
OLLAMA_VERSION=0.35.0
OLLAMA_TAG=v0.35.0
OLLAMA_TAG_COMMIT=cc4069396f3ad2c370c53eed2e4a42ac13adab84
OLLAMA_ASSET=ollama-linux-arm64.tar.zst
OLLAMA_ASSET_SHA256=cb627d332b1fe5055bd5485ca10d595da8429e447648209e375390ec3bd09374

# Ollama's MIT licence, fetched from the tag (the release tarball carries only the third-party licences).
OLLAMA_LICENSE_SHA256=5934ed2ce0d15154bcdb9c85203210abac0da4314af34081e36df4599f90b226

# The Debian bookworm base of the node22 runtime (glibc 2.36). Only used for the smoke test; it is the runtime Dockerfile's own
# digest, read from runtimes/node22/Dockerfile by build.sh.
